      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Every loose round in the LV press is two small GregTech parts plus gunpowder. The case is a foil: a thin brass sheet made in the Bending Machine. The slug is a round: a small metal ball made in a Lathe from a nugget, or by hand with a file. Lead rounds go into pistol bullets and shotgun pellets; steel rounds go into rifle bullets.\n\nHold sixteen brass foils, sixteen lead rounds and sixteen steel rounds to finish. Each recipe takes sixteen of a part, so that is one run\u0027s worth of each. Brass is a copper and zinc alloy; check NEI for how to make it.\n\n[note]Make plenty. A single 9mm batch eats sixteen of each part.[/note]",
